The `src/act/properties/` directory used raw `FILE *debug` (GROMACS global) and `FILE*` parameters for debug output, inconsistent with the `MsgHandler`-based pattern used elsewhere in the codebase.

## Changes

### `src/act/properties/`
- **`b2data.h/cpp`**: `dump(FILE*)` → `dump(MsgHandler*)`, using `std::ostringstream` + `writeDebug()`
- **`rotator.h/cpp`**: `checkMatrix(FILE*)` and `printAverageMatrix(FILE*)` → `MsgHandler*` variants using `writeDebug()`; pre-computes `1/naver_` to avoid repeated division
- **`dimergenerator.h/cpp`**: Added `msghandler_` member; stored from `generate()`/`generateDimers()` calls so the destructor can call `printAverageMatrix(msghandler_)` instead of `printAverageMatrix(stdout)`
- **`normalmodes.cpp`, `simulate.cpp`, `secondvirial.cpp`**: Replaced `if (debug) { topology()->dump(debug); }` with `if (msghandler.debug()) { topology()->dump(msghandler.twDebug()); }`

### `src/act/alexandria/`
- **`topology.h/cpp`**: Added `dump(gmx::TextWriter*)` overload (writes via `tw->writeLine()`) to support the callers above; only the debug `TextWriter` is needed, so the full `MsgHandler` is not passed

```cpp
// Before
if (debug)
{
    actmol.topology()->dump(debug);
}

// After
if (msghandler.debug())
{
    actmol.topology()->dump(msghandler.twDebug());
}
```

Standalone document directory tree component with expand/collapse, inline rename, context menu operations, and drag-and-drop reordering.

### Component API

```js
DocTree.init('#container', {
  syncData: async (action, reqData) => {
    // action: 'init' | 'add_child' | 'add_sibling' | 'rename' | 'copy' | 'delete' | 'move'
    return { tree: [...], error: "", success: true };
  },
  container: { maxHeight: '500px', width: '300px' },
  enableDrag: true
});
```

### Implementation

- **Recursive template generation** — `_nodeTemplate(depth)` generates nested Alpine.js `x-for` loops (up to 10 levels) at init time, using variable scope shadowing (`node in node.children`) to achieve recursion within Alpine's template constraints
- **Tree operations** — All mutations (add child/sibling, copy, rename, delete, move) go through the configurable `syncData` callback, with optimistic UI updates and rollback on failure
- **Drag-and-drop** — Sortable.js with `group` option on nested `<ul>` elements for cross-level node movement; Sortable instances are re-initialized after tree mutations and expand/collapse
- **State preservation** — `_applyTree()` collects expanded node IDs before replacing tree data, restoring expand state across server-synced updates
- **Editing guard** — `_editingBusy` flag prevents double-fire from blur + enter on rename input

### Demo

`doc-tree.html` includes a self-contained mock backend with full CRUD operations — open directly in browser.

Clicking "▶ 开始追踪" appeared unresponsive because the button could get stuck in a permanently disabled state. Three bugs in `docs/netfilter-trace-animation.html`:

## Fixes

- **Button never re-enabled on `run()` error** — `anim.run().catch()` only logged the error; `showFinal()` and `setCtrlState('done')` were never called, leaving the button disabled forever on any animation exception
  ```js
  // before
  anim.run().catch(e=>console.warn(e));
  // after
  anim.run().catch(e=>{console.warn(e);setCtrlState('idle');});
  ```

- **`stop()` leaked timers** — `clearTimeout` was never called on the pending `wait()` timer; old animation timers fired hundreds of milliseconds after `stop()`, potentially corrupting DOM state for a newly started animation

  ```js
  stop(){
    this.stopped=true; this.paused=false;
    if(this._pendingTimer){clearTimeout(this._pendingTimer); this._pendingTimer=null;}
    if(this._res){this._res(); this._res=null;}
  }
  ```

- **`doStartTrace()` didn't stop previous animation** — replaced the `anim` reference without calling `stop()` on the old instance; now explicitly stops and nulls any prior animation before validation and re-simulation

This update aligns the chat UI with the requested product messaging and interaction flow: explicit synthetic-content disclaimer, stronger upgrade affordances, and replacement of “Ready/dot/ms” status patterns with inline AI thinking/streaming behavior.

- **Policy and legal footer copy**
  - Replaced the compact footer links text with a full disclaimer message:
    - “eSAMz AI generates synthetic content and may be inaccurate…”
  - Kept direct links to Privacy Policy and Terms in the same footer location.

- **Plans discoverability and upgrade conversion**
  - Updated sidebar action copy from “View Plans” to **“View Plans & Upgrade”**.
  - Strengthened plans modal primary CTA copy to emphasize upgrade value.
  - Added premium-oriented feature bullets (Pro/Max) and enhanced CTA/button visual emphasis to make higher tiers more compelling.

- **Status model simplification (remove Ready/ms/dot UI)**
  - Removed header status pill usage (`Ready`, green dot, processing indicator).
  - Removed connection ping latency display and related quality-dot color logic.
  - Eliminated associated status update plumbing in client logic.

- **AI response loading and streaming behavior**
  - Replaced three-dot typing loader with a text loader (`Thinking…` / `Writing…`) in the answer area.
  - Switched to paced progressive rendering so responses appear as a controlled stream instead of arriving in large chunks.
  - Extracted streaming speed thresholds/interval into named constants and helper logic for readability and tuning.

```tsx
const TYPEWRITER_INTERVAL_MS = 18;

const getTypewriterChunkSize = (remaining: number) => {
  if (remaining > 160) return 10;
  if (remaining > 80) return 6;
  if (remaining > 30) return 3;
  return 2;
};
```

