After the atomic claim transaction sets `isThinking: true`, any unhandled exception in the subsequent Firestore reads (API key, player config, public settings) left the game permanently stuck in processing state — no move forwarded, no analysis performed, no error surfaced.

## Changes

- **`api/ai-move.js` / `functions/index.js`**: Wrap the entire post-claim processing block in a `try/catch`. On any unhandled error, the catch resets `isThinking: false`, clears `thinkingPlayer` and `currentThinkingText`, and writes an `error` field to Firestore so the UI can surface it.

```js
} catch (err) {
  console.error(`[ai-move] Unhandled error for match ${matchId}:`, err)
  await gsRef.update({
    isThinking: false,
    thinkingPlayer: null,
    currentThinkingText: '',
    error: `Internal error: ${err.message}`,
  }).catch((recoveryErr) => console.error(`[ai-move] Failed to reset isThinking for match ${matchId}:`, recoveryErr))
  return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error.' })
}
```

The already-existing `try/catch` around `callOpenRouter` remains in place; this new outer guard covers the unprotected setup phase that precedes it.
